#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# take_smallest

#% text
# `take_smallest(xs, n)` gives the `n` smallest elements of `xs`, smallest first.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Elements are compared in the canonical order, so numbers by value.

#% item
# `take_largest` gives the largest ones.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
take_smallest([3, 1, 4, 1, 5], 2)
#% output
#= [1, 1]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The first elements of `sort`:

#% cell
xs = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]
take_smallest(xs, 3) == take(sort(xs), 3)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `take_largest`, `sort`, `min`, `min_by`
